OL,3,GNEWSAAnonymous donor gives girl 'second
OL,4,Achance at life'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman from Coventry has been given
OL,7,Fpotentially life-saving treatment after
OL,8,Fbeing diagnosed with acute leukaemia in
OL,9,FJune.
OL,11,FLilly Dye received a stem cell
OL,12,Ftransplant from an anonymous donor
OL,13,Fafter going through chemotherapy
OL,14,Ftreatment at Queen Elizabeth Hospital
OL,15,FBirmingham.
OL,17,FHer mother, Claire Attwood, said that
OL,18,Fher daughter's diagnosis took the
OL,19,Ffamily by shock, but that they are
OL,20,Funbelievably thankful to the donor.
OL,23,APub: 09-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,353,350,200,160,0,100
